# Signed governance-frontier evidence, published as one unit. The manifest is
# Ed25519-signed by the key in trusted-publisher.pub and pins SHA-256 digests
# of the source tree it was measured from, so a hunk-level merge produces a
# manifest whose signature and digests match nothing -- and it does so
# silently, because the pieces all look plausible. Any change under
# packages/maverick-core/maverick or packages/maverick-shield/maverick_shield
# invalidates the digests, so two branches touching the kernel will both
# republish these and collide. `-merge` makes git stop at a whole-file
# conflict rather than interleaving them.
#
# Resolve by taking one side entire (never a mixture), then run
# `python benchmarks/eval_governance_frontier.py --verify-tracked-artifacts`.
# If that fails, re-measure with a plain `python
# benchmarks/eval_governance_frontier.py` from a clean tree; do not hand-edit.
/benchmarks/results/governance-frontier-v1/measured-manifest.json text eol=lf -merge
/benchmarks/results/governance-frontier-v1/trusted-publisher.pub text eol=lf -merge
/benchmarks/results/governance-frontier-v1/verify_manifest.py text eol=lf
/benchmarks/GOVERNANCE_FRONTIER_RESULTS.md text eol=lf -merge
